+## M16 GPU firmware incident: proposed rollback
+
+The private M16 ISO `20261101T183232Z` with kernel `7.3.0-65.sp11.14.fc44` produced repeated `msm_dpu` vblank timeout warnings from `drm_fb_helper_damage_work`; an earlier DIE was photographed only in part, without its header. The operator reports this loop was absent in M15.1. M16 commit `2ee4dbf` added the SQE, GMU and zap firmware to the initramfs, allowing the early DRM client open to succeed. The proposed mitigation restores the earlier policy: retain all three on the rootfs, remove their explicit initramfs installation, and fail L0 5.8 if dracut includes any of them anyway. The build record states this policy. This is a proposed cause and mitigation, not proof of the cause of the DIE or of a successful device boot.
+
+`msm_open()` calls `load_gpu()` on each open (Linux `sources/linux/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c:266`); `adreno_load_gpu()` returns on a firmware load failure (`sources/linux/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_device.c:87`). A later userspace open can therefore retry after switch-root with the rootfs firmware available; actual GPU and desktop operation remain device tests. The early in-kernel client is expected to fail its open as in M15.1, so early msm fbcon is unavailable and the screen may be blank until a later display client initializes it. The collector does not depend on fbcon: its systemd service captures the journal and dmesg and writes to the boot medium; dracut failure hooks capture early failures separately. Neither path guarantees a capture if the kernel dies before it runs. An alternative is to retain the early firmware and add `drm_kms_helper.fbdev_emulation=0` to affected entries; that changes kernel command lines and requires separate validation. No GRUB arguments change in this proposal.
+
+Reference comparison: `/tmp/ref-sp11` was unavailable in this environment, so the upstream [reference tree](https://github.com/dwhinham/archiso-aarch64-sp11/tree/9a50ce3c81e4e17b30adcfc0dd517c19795e89f3) at `9a50ce3c81e4e17b30adcfc0dd517c19795e89f3` was inspected instead. Its `configs/releng/profiledef.sh` sets `clk_ignore_unused pd_ignore_unused arm64.nopauth systemd.mask=tpm2.target`; `configs/releng/airootfs/etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/archiso.conf` includes `msm` and `panel_edp` with the `kms` hook. Its README says proprietary firmware is not redistributed and instructs users to run `sp11-grab-fw` after installation. This is a different distribution and kernel, and does not establish our runtime outcome.
+
+Audio review: the M16 speaker UCM service copies userspace ALSA configuration on `debug`, `safe` and `spk`; the copy operation itself cannot execute kernel code or directly cause a kernel DIE. ALSA clients may later apply that configuration through kernel audio interfaces, so an indirect trigger cannot be excluded from the incomplete DIE transcript. M16 also changes `cdsp-experiment` permission detection; that service can restart CDSP and change kernel-exposed parameters and firmware selection, so its interaction with kernel/DSP paths cannot be ruled out from image inspection. Preserve speaker safety gates and obtain the full DIE header and stack before attribution.
+
